        q: "Can PoS nudges for energy eficiencia backfire?",
        a: "Yes, poorly designed nudges can produce reactance effects where consumers deliberately choose the non-nudged option to assert autonomy. Overly aggressive or patronizing framing is particularly counterproductive. Additionally, nudges that highlight price premiums for efficient products may inadvertently anchor price-sensitive consumers on costo rather than value, reducing adoption rates.",
