        q: "What geographic resolution can PoS-based economic indicators achieve?",
        a: "The achievable resolution depends on the density of PoS-adopting businesses in a given area. In urban areas with high PoS penetration, neighborhood-level indicators covering a few city blocks are feasible. In areas with lower penetration, district or municipal-level aggregation may be the finest practical resolution. Minimum-count thresholds for privacy protection also limit the granularity achievable in sparse areas.",
