        q: "How can a small minoristaer test pricing strategies without sophisticated análisis tools?",
        a: "A practical approach is sequential testing: change the price of a high-volume item for a defined period (at least two to four weeks to capture day-of-week variation), then compare ventas volume and ingresos against the equivalent preceding period. Controlling for seasonal effects by testing during similar calendar periods improves reliability. Testing one item at a time prevents confounding.",
